Starter PIDoc source for Astro Color Mixer v0.9.3-beta. Formal PixInsight documentation integration to be validated.

\title Astro Color Mixer Technical Appendix

\section Introduction

This appendix summarizes the practical processing model used by Astro Color Mixer for nonlinear RGB astrophotography refinement.

\section Design Goals

- controlled nonlinear RGB refinement
- astro-specific color-band workflow
- reduced arbitrary global color swings
- support for stars-present and starless workflows
- visible masks and diagnostics
- non-destructive output-to-new-image behavior

\section Processing Assumptions

- nonlinear RGB input
- normalized internal RGB values in the range 0..1
- source image not overwritten
- preview uses downsampled data
- final Apply uses full-resolution data

\section Image Type

Stars Present is more conservative around bright stellar structures. Starless / Star-Reduced allows more freedom in nebulae, galaxies, dust, and faint structures. This setting does not detect stars, remove stars, or create a star mask.

\section Luminance Model

Y = 0.2126 R + 0.7152 G + 0.0722 B

Luminance is used for Range Mask, diagnostics, neutral luminance, and protection terms.

\section Hue and Saturation Selection

Hue is circular and low saturation makes hue unreliable. Band selection uses circular hue distance around practical astro band centers.

\section Astro Color Bands

- red 0 deg
- orange 30 deg
- yellow 60 deg
- green 120 deg
- cyan 180 deg
- blue 240 deg
- purple 275 deg
- magenta 315 deg

These are practical editing regions, not strict physical line definitions.

\section Hue Band Mask

distance = circularHueDistance(hue, center)
mask = 1 - smoothstep(innerWidth, outerWidth, distance)

\section Saturation Reliability

Low-saturation pixels are prevented from behaving like stable hue targets, which is why the tool includes a separate Neutral / Low-Saturation luminance path.

\section Range Mask

leftRamp = smoothstep(low - feather, low, Y)
rightRamp = 1 - smoothstep(high, high + feather, Y)
rangeMask = clamp01(leftRamp * rightRamp)

\section Neutral / Low-Saturation

neutralMask = 1 - smoothstep(satStart, satFull, saturation)

\section Chroma-Vector Adjustment

Conceptually, the tool separates a luminance-like neutral component from chroma, scales saturation, rotates hue, adjusts luminance, recombines the result, and clamps back into a valid nonlinear RGB range.

\section Combined Mask

finalMask =
  hueMask *
  saturationReliability *
  darkProtection *
  highlightProtection *
  rangeMask

\section Refinement Passes

working = original
for each enabled pass:
    working = applyPass(working, pass)

\section Limitations

- not intended for linear calibration
- preview is approximate
- hue is unreliable in neutral areas
- Range Mask depends on stretch
- saturated star cores require care
- beta software status applies
